IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nad-dates`
IMPORT `nad-rules`

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) -- the questions of the PERSON AGGRIEVED (the complainant).
--
-- SEAT: the individual who has been treated badly and may complain to the Anti-Discrimination Commissioner -- a worker
-- or job applicant, a student, a tenant or would-be tenant, a customer, a club member, a person seeking insurance or
-- superannuation, a person dealing with a Territory agency: "Was I discriminated against?", "Was I sexually harassed?",
-- "Was I victimised for complaining?", "Can they rely on an exemption?", "Can I hold the employer liable too?", "Can I
-- complain, and by when?", "By when must I ask for a hearing, and appeal?", "What can the Tribunal order?". The
-- respondent, the Commissioner, the Tribunal and the Supreme Court get no seat: their judgments and decisions are asked
-- as facts. An exemption is something the respondent must prove (s 91(2)); it is asked here as "does it cover what they
-- did?", on facts the person aggrieved may know or be told.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of nad-rules.l4.
-- Four regulative rules -- the time limit for the complaint (s 65), the strict limit for an old s 20A complaint
-- (s 126(2)), the reply to a lapse notice (s 72) and the request for referral (s 81) -- are DEONTIC rules run inside
-- the "on this day" questions; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- The questions on what happened and on exemptions assume conduct on or after 3 July 2023 (and, for s 20A, on or after
-- 31 October 2025) and a complaint made on or after 27 July 2026: the first question says which version applies.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT). Copyright in Northern Territory
-- legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the Northern Territory copyright policy of 8 October 1996;
-- see SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT): the questions of the person aggrieved`

§§ `Which version of the Act applies to me`

@export Which version of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) applies to what happened to me (ss 116, 122, 123, 126, 128)? The Act does not reach conduct before 1 August 1993; conduct before 3 July 2023, or a complaint made before then, is governed by the Act as it then stood; inciting hatred (s 20A) before 31 October 2025 is governed by the old s 20A; and a pending complaint made before 27 July 2026 is dealt with under Part 6 as it then stood.
GIVEN `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct you complain of took place (for continuing conduct, the latest day)
      `is it about inciting hatred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your complaint is about an act inciting hatred, serious contempt or severe ridicule of you or your group because of an attribute (s 20A)
      `have I already complained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already made a complaint to the Anti-Discrimination Commissioner about it that is still being dealt with
      `the day I complained` IS A DATE @desc The day you made that complaint (any date if you have not)
GIVETH A `Which law applies`
`Which version of the Act applies to me` MEANS
    `transitional -- which law applies` `the day it happened` `is it about inciting hatred` `have I already complained` `the day I complained`

§§ `What happened to me`

@export Is the reason they treated me badly an "attribute" protected by the Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) (s 19(1), s 4)? The Act protects race, language, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, sex characteristics, age, relationship status, accommodation status, employment status, sex work, pregnancy, carer responsibilities, breastfeeding, disability, HIV/hepatitis status, being subjected to domestic violence, union or employer association activity, religious belief or activity, political opinion, an irrelevant medical or criminal record, publication of fine default details, and association with a person who has one of these. Nothing else counts.
GIVEN `the reason` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute you were treated badly for, whether you have it, had it, or are believed to have it (or something else not listed)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it a protected attribute` MEANS `s 19 -- it is an attribute` `the reason`

@export Was I discriminated against under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) (ss 19, 20, 21, 28 and Part 4), before any exemption they may rely on? Discrimination is treating you less favourably than someone without your attribute because of it (it need not be the only or main reason, and their motive does not matter), a distinction, restriction, exclusion or preference that impairs your equality of opportunity, or harassment because of it, in education, work, accommodation, goods and services, clubs, insurance and superannuation, or the administration of Territory laws and programs. Less favourable treatment because of an assistance animal is disability discrimination.
GIVEN `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute you were treated badly for (you have it, had it, or are believed to have it, or a characteristic is imputed to it)
      `the area` IS AN `Area` @desc Where it happened: education; work (being hired, the terms of work, promotion, training, dismissal or other treatment of a worker); a professional, trade or employer organisation; a body granting a qualification or licence for a trade or profession; an employment agency; accommodation; goods, services or facilities; a club; insurance or superannuation; the administration of a Territory law or government program; or none of these
      `how many members the club has` IS A NUMBER @desc If it was a club: how many members it has (the Act's clubs have at least 30); any number otherwise
      `treated less favourably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they treated you, or proposed to treat you, less favourably than they treat or would treat a person without the attribute, because of the attribute
      `a distinction impairing my equality of opportunity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they made a distinction, restriction, exclusion or preference on the basis of the attribute that nullified or impaired your equality of opportunity
      `harassed because of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were harassed on the basis of the attribute
      `because of my assistance animal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a disability and were treated less favourably because you have an assistance animal (an animal trained or accredited to help you in public with your disability)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I discriminated against` MEANS
    `ss 19-21 -- I was discriminated against` `the attribute` `the area` `how many members the club has` `treated less favourably` `a distinction impairing my equality of opportunity` `harassed because of it` `because of my assistance animal`

@export Was I sexually harassed under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 22? It is unwelcome physical intimacy, an unwelcome demand or request for sexual favours, an unwelcome remark with sexual connotations, or other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature, done to offend, humiliate or intimidate you, or where a reasonable person would have anticipated you might be offended, humiliated or intimidated, or where you would (or reasonably believed you would) suffer a detriment if you objected.
GIVEN `what they did` IS A `Sexual conduct` @desc What they did: an act of physical intimacy; a demand or request for sexual favours, direct or implied; a remark with sexual connotations; other conduct of a sexual nature; or none of these
      `was it unwelcome` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was unwelcome to you
      `did they mean to offend me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they did it with the intention of offending, humiliating or intimidating you
      `would a reasonable person have anticipated offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person would have anticipated the possibility that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated (taking into account your race, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, sex characteristics, age, relationship status, religion, any disability, your relationship with them and your other circumstances)
      `detriment if I objected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would suffer, or reasonably believed you were likely to suffer, some detriment if you objected
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I sexually harassed` MEANS
    `s 22 -- I was sexually harassed` `what they did` `was it unwelcome` `did they mean to offend me` `would a reasonable person have anticipated offence` `detriment if I objected`

@export Was I victimised under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 23? It is subjecting you or your associate to a detriment, or threatening to, because you complained or intend to, gave or intend to give evidence or information in proceedings under the Act, alleged or intend to allege a contravention of the Act (unless the allegation is false and not made in good faith), or did anything else under or by reference to the Act.
GIVEN `a detriment to me or my associate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they subjected you or an associate of yours to a detriment, or threatened to
      `why they did it` IS A `Reason for the detriment` @desc Why they did it: because you made or intend to make a complaint; gave or intend to give evidence or information in proceedings under the Act; alleged or intend to allege a contravention of the Act; did something else under or by reference to the Act; or another reason
      `was my allegation false and not in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was because of an allegation: whether the allegation was false and not made in good faith
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I victimised` MEANS
    `s 23 -- I was victimised` `a detriment to me or my associate` `why they did it` `was my allegation false and not in good faith`

@export Did they break their duty to reasonably accommodate a special need I have because of an attribute (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 24)? For example, providing an accredited interpreter to a person who needs one. Whether they reasonably provided for it depends on the need, the cost and how many people benefit or are disadvantaged, their finances, the disruption, and the benefit or detriment to everyone (s 24(3)).
GIVEN `a special need because of an attribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a special need because of an attribute (for example a disability, pregnancy, or language)
      `did they reasonably provide for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they made adequate or appropriate provision that reasonably provided for your special need
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Did they fail to accommodate my special need` MEANS
    `s 24 -- they failed to accommodate my special need` `a special need because of an attribute` `did they reasonably provide for it`

@export Must my landlord or accommodation provider let me alter the accommodation to meet my needs as a person with a disability (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 39)? Yes if the alteration is at your expense, needs no alteration to anyone else's accommodation, can reasonably be undone, and you undertake to restore it at your expense before you leave and are reasonably likely to.
GIVEN `I have a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a disability
      `at my expense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the alteration is to be made at your own expense
      `no one else's accommodation altered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the alteration does not require any alteration to another person's accommodation
      `can it reasonably be undone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether restoring the accommodation to its previous condition is reasonably practicable
      `will I restore it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you undertake to restore it at your own expense before leaving, and are reasonably likely to do so
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must they let me alter the accommodation` MEANS
    `s 39 -- they must allow the alteration` `I have a disability` `at my expense` `no one else's accommodation altered` `can it reasonably be undone` `will I restore it`

@export Was the advertisement prohibited (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 25)? A person must not publish, cause to be published or authorise the publication of an advertisement that promotes or expresses, or could reasonably be understood to promote or express, prohibited conduct or an intention to engage in it. Discriminatory advertising is prohibited conduct (s 4), so you may complain about it.
GIVEN `did they publish it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person complained about published an advertisement, caused it to be published or authorised its publication
      `does it promote discrimination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the advertisement promotes or expresses, or could reasonably be understood to promote or express, prohibited conduct (such as discrimination against people with an attribute) or an intention to engage in it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was the advertisement prohibited` MEANS
    `s 25 -- the advertisement was prohibited` `did they publish it` `does it promote discrimination`

@export They asked me for information (for example on a form or in an interview): was that prohibited under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 26? It is, if unlawful discrimination might be based on the information, unless the request was necessary to comply with or specifically authorised by a Territory or Commonwealth law, a court or tribunal order, an award, an industrial agreement or an order of the Commissioner, or they prove the information was reasonably required for a purpose not involving discrimination.
GIVEN `could discrimination be based on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information is something on which unlawful discrimination might be based (for example your age, religion, pregnancy or relationship status)
      `required or authorised by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request was necessary to comply with, or specifically authorised by, a Territory or Commonwealth law, a court or tribunal order, an award, an industrial agreement or an order of the Commissioner
      `did they prove a non-discriminatory need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they prove, on the balance of probabilities, that the information was reasonably required for a purpose that did not involve discrimination
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was asking me for that information prohibited` MEANS
    `s 26 -- asking me was prohibited` `could discrimination be based on it` `required or authorised by law` `did they prove a non-discriminatory need`

@export Was the act inciting hatred, serious contempt or severe ridicule of me or my group prohibited (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) ss 20A, 20B)? It is prohibited if it was reasonably likely to incite hatred, serious contempt or severe ridicule and was done because of an attribute, unless done in private, or said or done reasonably and in good faith for an artistic work, a genuine academic, artistic, scientific or public interest purpose, a fair and accurate report, or a fair comment expressing a genuine belief. For acts before 31 October 2025 the old s 20A applies.
GIVEN `reasonably likely to incite` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act was reasonably likely, in all the circumstances, to incite hatred towards, serious contempt for or severe ridicule of you or a group you belong to
      `because of an attribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was done because of an attribute of you or of some or all of the people in the group
      `communicated to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it caused words, sounds, images or writing to be communicated to the public (for example online or in print)
      `in a public place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was done in a public place (any place the public may enter, as of right or by invitation, paid or not)
      `seen or heard from a public place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was done in the sight or hearing of people in a public place
      `otherwise in private` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, apart from those, it was done in private
      `reasonably and in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was said or done reasonably and in good faith
      `its purpose` IS A `Purpose under s 20B` @desc Whether it was in an artistic work; a statement, publication, discussion or debate for a genuine academic, artistic, scientific or public interest purpose; a fair and accurate report of a matter of public interest; a fair comment expressing a genuine belief; or none of these
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was the act inciting hatred prohibited` MEANS
    `s 20A -- the act was prohibited` `reasonably likely to incite` `because of an attribute` `communicated to the public` `in a public place` `seen or heard from a public place` `otherwise in private` `reasonably and in good faith` `its purpose`

§§ `Who else I can hold liable`

@export Is the person who caused, instructed, induced, incited, assisted or promoted the contravention liable with the person who did it (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 27)? They are jointly and severally liable with that person.
GIVEN `did they cause or help it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they caused, instructed, induced, incited, assisted or promoted the other person to do it
      `did the other person contravene the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person's conduct contravened the Act (for example discrimination, sexual harassment or victimisation with no exemption)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the person who caused or helped it liable too` MEANS
    `s 27 -- they are jointly liable` `did they cause or help it` `did the other person contravene the Act`

@export Is the employer or principal liable as if they had done it themselves, when their worker or agent discriminated against, harassed or victimised me (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 105)? Yes, unless they show they took all reasonable steps to prevent it (training, an equal opportunity plan, a published policy, given their finances and size).
GIVEN `was it their worker or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who did it was a worker (employee, contractor, volunteer or other) or an agent of the employer or principal
      `in connection with the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was done in connection with the employer's work, or the agent's duties as an agent
      `was it unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act was unlawful under the Act (prohibited conduct with no exemption)
      `did they take all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer or principal shows that they took all reasonable steps to prevent it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the employer or principal liable too` MEANS
    `s 105 -- they are liable as if they had done it` `was it their worker or agent` `in connection with the work` `was it unlawful` `did they take all reasonable steps`

§§ `Exemptions they may rely on`

-- An exemption makes the discrimination lawful (s 19(2)). The respondent must raise it and prove it on the balance of
-- probabilities (s 91(2)). Each question asks only about the exemption they rely on.

@export Does an exemption for work cover what my employer or prospective employer did (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) ss 35, 35A, 35B, 36, 37, 127)? The exemptions: reasonable terms for a restricted capacity because of age or disability; a genuine occupational qualification; inability to do the inherent requirements even with your special need accommodated; offering work in their own home; employment status in hiring, if reasonable, justifiable and proportionate; a religious school's preference on religious grounds, in good faith and under a written policy (not for staff already there on 31 October 2025); a standard starting or retirement age; an irrelevant criminal record for work caring for vulnerable people, if reasonably necessary. They must prove it.
GIVEN `which exemption` IS A `Work exemption` @desc The exemption they rely on
      `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute the discrimination was on
      `in offering work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was in deciding who should be offered work, the terms of work offered, or failing or refusing to offer work (rather than treatment of a worker already working)
      `restricted capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of age or disability, you have a restricted capacity to do the work
      `are the terms reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the terms and conditions they fixed for you are reasonable
      `a genuine occupational qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is based on a genuine occupational qualification you are required to fill
      `unable to do the inherent requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are unable to adequately perform the inherent requirements of the work even with your special need accommodated
      `work in their home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is to be performed in their home
      `reasonable, justifiable and proportionate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is reasonable, justifiable and proportionate in the circumstances
      `a religious school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is the authority of an educational institution run in accordance with the doctrine of a particular religion
      `in good faith for religious sensitivities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was in good faith to avoid offending the religious sensitivities of a reasonable person of that religion
      `written policy available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the school produced a written policy setting out the doctrine it relies on and made it available to employees and prospective employees
      `I worked for an educational institution on 31 October 2025` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were working for an educational institution (this one or any other) on 31 October 2025, when s 35B commenced (s 127)
      `a standard age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they imposed a standard age for starting work or a standard retirement age
      `caring for vulnerable people` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work principally involves the care, instruction or supervision of vulnerable persons (children, aged persons, people with a disability or mental illness)
      `reasonably necessary to protect them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is reasonably necessary to protect their physical, psychological or emotional well-being, having regard to all the circumstances including your actions
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does a work exemption cover it` MEANS
    `ss 35-37 -- the work exemption applies` `which exemption` `the attribute` `in offering work` `restricted capacity` `are the terms reasonable` `a genuine occupational qualification` `unable to do the inherent requirements` `work in their home` `reasonable, justifiable and proportionate` `a religious school` `in good faith for religious sensitivities` `written policy available` `I worked for an educational institution on 31 October 2025` `a standard age` `caring for vulnerable people` `reasonably necessary to protect them`

@export Does an exemption for education or accommodation cover what they did (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) ss 30, 40)? The exemptions: a single-sex school, or a school for students with a disability, excluding applicants; deciding who lives in their own or a near relative's home; school accommodation for one sex or for students with a disability; accommodation of a religious body at a place of worship, in accordance with doctrine and necessary to avoid offence (not while a government-funded program runs there); accommodation of a charitable body in accordance with its purpose. They must prove it.
GIVEN `which exemption` IS AN `Education or accommodation exemption` @desc The exemption they rely on
      `a school for one sex` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the educational institution is wholly or mainly for students of one sex
      `I am not of that sex` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are not of that sex
      `a school for a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the educational institution is wholly or mainly for students with a general or specific disability
      `I do not have that disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do not have that disability
      `about my admission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was about your application for admission as a student
      `accommodation for those students` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accommodation is provided wholly or mainly for students of that sex, or with that disability
      `their or a near relative's home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was deciding who is to live in accommodation that is, and is to remain, part of the main home of the provider or their parent, child, grandparent, sibling or spouse or partner
      `run by a religious body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accommodation is under the direction or control of a body established for religious purposes
      `at a place of worship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is wholly within or directly attached to a church, temple, synagogue, mosque or similar place of worship
      `in accordance with doctrine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is in accordance with the doctrine of the religion
      `necessary to avoid offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is necessary to avoid offending the religious sensitivities of people of the religion
      `a government program there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Territory or Commonwealth funded program was being conducted at the accommodation at the time
      `run by a charitable body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accommodation is under the direction or control of a body established for a charitable purpose
      `in accordance with its purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is in accordance with the particular purpose for which the body established the accommodation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does an education or accommodation exemption cover it` MEANS
    `ss 30, 40 -- the exemption applies` `which exemption` `a school for one sex` `I am not of that sex` `a school for a disability` `I do not have that disability` `about my admission` `accommodation for those students` `their or a near relative's home` `run by a religious body` `at a place of worship` `in accordance with doctrine` `necessary to avoid offence` `a government program there` `run by a charitable body` `in accordance with its purpose`

@export Does an exemption for goods, services and facilities cover what they did (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) ss 42-45)? The exemptions: a service that by its nature only one sex can receive; restricting access to a place of cultural or religious significance by sex, age, race or religion, in accordance with the culture or doctrine and necessary to avoid offence; age-based benefits and concessions; requiring a child under 18 to be accompanied by an adult where there is a reasonable risk of disruption or danger. They must prove it.
GIVEN `which exemption` IS A `Goods and services exemption` @desc The exemption they rely on
      `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute the discrimination was on
      `a one-sex service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service by its nature can only be provided to members of one sex
      `a place of cultural or religious significance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they restricted access to land, a building or a place of cultural or religious significance
      `in accordance with culture or doctrine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the restriction is in accordance with the culture or the doctrine of the religion
      `necessary to avoid offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is necessary to avoid offending the cultural or religious sensitivities of people of the culture or religion
      `an age-based benefit or concession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they were supplying benefits or concessions on the basis of age
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `must be accompanied by an adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they required, as a term of supply, that you be accompanied by an adult
      `a reasonable risk if unaccompanied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a reasonable risk that a child could cause a disruption or endanger themselves or others if not accompanied by an adult
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does a goods and services exemption cover it` MEANS
    `ss 42-45 -- the exemption applies` `which exemption` `the attribute` `a one-sex service` `a place of cultural or religious significance` `in accordance with culture or doctrine` `necessary to avoid offence` `an age-based benefit or concession` `my age` `must be accompanied by an adult` `a reasonable risk if unaccompanied`

@export Does an exemption for clubs cover what the club did (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 47)? The exemptions: refusing applicants outside the group the club was established for, if it operates mainly to preserve a minority culture or for that group's disadvantage or needs; age, in membership of a club mainly for an age group; sex, in the use of a benefit the sexes cannot practicably share, where an equivalent separate benefit or a fair share is provided. They must prove it.
GIVEN `which exemption` IS A `Club exemption` @desc The exemption they rely on
      `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute the discrimination was on
      `I applied to join` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were applying for membership of the club
      `I am outside the club's group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are not a member of the group of people with an attribute for whom the club was established
      `the club serves a minority culture or the group's needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the club operates wholly or mainly to preserve a minority culture, or to prevent or reduce disadvantage suffered by, or meet the special needs of, that group
      `about membership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was about membership of the club
      `a club for an age group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the club provides association wholly or mainly for people of a specific age or age group
      `about the use of a club benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was about the use or enjoyment of a benefit the club provides
      `cannot be shared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is not practicable for the benefit to be used or enjoyed at the same time, or to the same extent, by different sexes
      `an equivalent or a fair share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the same or an equivalent benefit is provided for each sex separately, or each sex is entitled to a fair and reasonable proportion of its use
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does a club exemption cover it` MEANS
    `s 47 -- the club exemption applies` `which exemption` `the attribute` `I applied to join` `I am outside the club's group` `the club serves a minority culture or the group's needs` `about membership` `a club for an age group` `about the use of a club benefit` `cannot be shared` `an equivalent or a fair share`

@export Does an exemption for insurance or superannuation cover what the insurer or fund did (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 49)? The exemptions: applying a standard under the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993; what the Sex Discrimination Act 1984 permits; complying with another Commonwealth Act; reliance on reasonable actuarial or statistical data (or, if there is none, other reasonable data, or if there is no data, other relevant factors) where the discrimination is reasonable; and a superannuation fund condition existing on 1 August 1993, for members who joined by 1 August 1994. They must prove it.
GIVEN `which exemption` IS AN `Insurance exemption` @desc The exemption they rely on
      `a SIS Act standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination happened because of a standard in force under the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 (Cth)
      `permitted by the Sex Discrimination Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is permitted under the Sex Discrimination Act 1984 (Cth)
      `to comply with another Commonwealth Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it happened to comply with, obtain the benefits of, or avoid penalties under another Commonwealth Act
      `reasonable actuarial data exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is reasonable actuarial or statistical data, from a source it is reasonable to rely on
      `other reasonable data exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is other data on which it is reasonable to rely
      `based on that data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination was based on that data
      `reasonable in light of the data and factors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is reasonable having regard to the data (if any) and other relevant factors
      `is it superannuation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it concerns superannuation (rather than insurance)
      `an existing fund condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is based on a condition of the fund that existed on 1 August 1993
      `the day I joined the fund` IS A DATE @desc The day you became a member of the fund
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does an insurance or superannuation exemption cover it` MEANS
    `s 49 -- the insurance exemption applies` `which exemption` `a SIS Act standard` `permitted by the Sex Discrimination Act` `to comply with another Commonwealth Act` `reasonable actuarial data exists` `other reasonable data exists` `based on that data` `reasonable in light of the data and factors` `is it superannuation` `an existing fund condition` `the day I joined the fund`

@export Does a general exemption cover what they did (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) ss 21(5), 50-59)? The exemptions: not producing evidence of an assistance animal when asked; a legal incapacity relevant to the transaction; religious ordination, training or observance; a charitable provision in a will or deed; acts necessary to comply with or authorised by a law, order, award, agreement or the Commissioner; rights given to someone else for pregnancy or childbirth; disability discrimination reasonably necessary to protect public health; restricting competitive sport by sex (if reasonable for strength, stamina or physique, and not for children under 12), ability, age or disability; special measures until equality is achieved; a special need that it would be unreasonable to accommodate; an exemption the Commissioner granted. They must prove it.
GIVEN `which exemption` IS A `General exemption` @desc The exemption they rely on
      `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute the discrimination was on
      `because of my animal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they discriminated against you because you have the animal
      `I did not produce evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they asked you for evidence that the animal is an assistance animal and you did not produce it
      `a legal incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are subject to a legal incapacity (for example being under 18 for a contract)
      `relevant to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that incapacity is relevant to the transaction
      `religious ordination, training or observance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it concerned the ordination, appointment or training of priests, ministers, members of a religious order or religious leaders, or a religious observance or practice (including an act of a religious body done as part of it)
      `a charitable provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a discriminatory provision for charitable benefits in a will, deed or other instrument, or an act required to give effect to one
      `necessary to comply with the law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act was necessary to comply with, or specifically authorised by, a Territory or Commonwealth Act or regulation, a court or tribunal order, an award, an industrial agreement existing on 1 August 1993, or an order, guideline, code or advice of the Commissioner
      `only because of rights for another's pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reason is that they granted rights or privileges to another person in connection with that person's pregnancy or childbirth
      `necessary for public health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is reasonably necessary to protect public health
      `restricting competitive sport` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they restricted who may take part in a competitive sporting activity
      `the restriction` IS A `Sport restriction` @desc The basis of the restriction: to one sex; to people who can effectively compete; to a specified age or age group; to people with a general or specific disability; or another basis
      `reasonable for strength, stamina or physique` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a restriction to one sex is reasonable having regard to the strength, stamina or physique the activity requires
      `for children under 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the activity is for children under 12
      `coaching, umpiring or administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was coaching, umpiring or refereeing, or administration of the sport (or a prescribed activity), rather than taking part
      `a special measures program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a program, plan or arrangement designed to promote equality of opportunity for a group who are disadvantaged or have a special need because of an attribute
      `equality achieved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether equality of opportunity for that group has been achieved
      `I need special services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would require special services or facilities
      `unreasonable to require them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is unreasonable to require them to supply those services or facilities (given their nature, the cost and number who benefit, their finances, disruption, and benefit or detriment to all)
      `a Commissioner's exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an exemption granted or renewed by the Commissioner (for at most 3 years at a time) was in force and covered the conduct
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does a general exemption cover it` MEANS
    `Part 5 -- the general exemption applies` `which exemption` `the attribute` `because of my animal` `I did not produce evidence` `a legal incapacity` `relevant to the transaction` `religious ordination, training or observance` `a charitable provision` `necessary to comply with the law` `only because of rights for another's pregnancy` `necessary for public health` `restricting competitive sport` `the restriction` `reasonable for strength, stamina or physique` `for children under 12` `coaching, umpiring or administration` `a special measures program` `equality achieved` `I need special services` `unreasonable to require them` `a Commissioner's exemption`

§§ `Making a complaint`

@export Can I (or we) make a complaint to the Anti-Discrimination Commissioner (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) ss 60, 66D, 66F, 71, 72, 81)? The person aggrieved, a person the Commissioner authorises in writing on their behalf, or an organisation about systemic discrimination may complain. A complaint about the same conduct cannot be made again after an earlier one was declined after assessment (only a representative complaint, with permission), declined because nothing more could be done or withdrawn (unless the Commissioner permits), or lapsed.
GIVEN `who is complaining` IS A `Who is complaining` @desc Who is making the complaint: you as the person aggrieved; a person the Commissioner has authorised in writing to complain on your behalf; an organisation or body complaining of systemic discrimination; or someone else
      `an earlier complaint` IS AN `Earlier complaint` @desc What happened to any earlier complaint by you about the same conduct
      `permission given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has given permission for the complaint to be made again
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I make a complaint` MEANS
    `s 60 -- the complaint may be made` `who is complaining` `an earlier complaint` `permission given`

@export By when must I make my complaint to the Anti-Discrimination Commissioner (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) ss 65, 126)? Within 12 months after the conduct (a representative complaint about systemic discrimination: 24 months after an instance of it). The Commissioner may accept a late complaint if satisfied it is appropriate, except a complaint about inciting hatred done before 31 October 2025. The complaint must be in writing, set out the conduct in detail and, as far as practicable, name the respondent (s 64).
GIVEN `a representative complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a representative complaint by an organisation about systemic discrimination
      `about inciting hatred before 31 October 2025` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint is about an act inciting hatred, serious contempt or severe ridicule (s 20A) done before 31 October 2025
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct took place (for a representative complaint, the day of an instance of the systemic discrimination)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I make my complaint` MEANS
    `s 65 -- the last day to complain` `a representative complaint` `about inciting hatred before 31 October 2025` `the day it happened`

@export If I make my complaint on a given day, is it in time (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) ss 65, 126)? In time on or before the last day; after it, the Commissioner may still accept it if satisfied that is appropriate, except for a complaint about inciting hatred done before 31 October 2025.
GIVEN `a representative complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a representative complaint by an organisation about systemic discrimination
      `about inciting hatred before 31 October 2025` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint is about an act inciting hatred, serious contempt or severe ridicule (s 20A) done before 31 October 2025
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct took place (for a representative complaint, the day of an instance of the systemic discrimination)
      `the day I complain` IS A DATE @desc The day you make, or will make, the complaint (lodge, send or transmit it to the Commissioner)
GIVETH A `Complaint timing`
`Is my complaint in time if made on this day` MEANS
    `s 65 -- the complaint is in time` `a representative complaint` `about inciting hatred before 31 October 2025` `the day it happened` `the day I complain`

@export By when must the Commissioner decide whether to accept or decline my complaint (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 66)? No later than 60 days after receiving it (90 days for a representative complaint). If it is declined you must be given written reasons, and you cannot complain again about the same conduct (s 66D).
GIVEN `a representative complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a representative complaint by an organisation about systemic discrimination
      `the day the Commissioner received it` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner received the complaint
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the Commissioner decide on my complaint` MEANS
    `s 66 -- the last day for the decision` `a representative complaint` `the day the Commissioner received it`

§§ `If the Commissioner writes that my complaint will lapse (only if this has happened to you)`

@export The Commissioner has written that my complaint will lapse unless I say I wish to continue: by when must I reply (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 72)? Within 60 days of being advised; otherwise the complaint lapses and you cannot complain again about the same conduct.
GIVEN `the day I was advised` IS A DATE @desc The day you were advised in writing that the complaint will lapse unless you say you wish to continue
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I say I wish to continue` MEANS
    `s 72 -- the last day to say I wish to continue` `the day I was advised`

@export If I tell the Commissioner on a given day that I wish to continue with my complaint, does it continue (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 72)? Yes within 60 days of being advised that it will lapse; after that the complaint has lapsed and you cannot complain again about the same conduct.
GIVEN `the day I was advised` IS A DATE @desc The day you were advised in writing that the complaint will lapse unless you say you wish to continue
      `the day I reply` IS A DATE @desc The day you indicate, or will indicate, that you wish to continue
GIVETH A `Continuing outcome`
`Does my complaint continue if I reply on this day` MEANS
    `s 72 -- the outcome` `the day I was advised` `the day I reply`

§§ `Conciliation (only if you have been directed to attend)`

@export What can happen to me if I do not attend a conciliation I was directed to attend (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) ss 79, 80)? Without a reasonable excuse, the Commissioner may dismiss your complaint and order you to pay the respondent's costs (recoverable as a judgment debt), and failing to comply is an offence with a maximum penalty of 100 penalty units.
GIVEN `was I directed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner directed you in writing to take part in a conciliation, specifying the time and place
      `did I comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you complied with the direction
      `a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a reasonable excuse for not complying
GIVETH A `Conciliation consequence`
`What happens if I do not attend conciliation` MEANS
    `ss 79, 80 -- what follows` `was I directed in writing` `did I comply` `a reasonable excuse`

§§ `Going to the Tribunal (only if conciliation did not resolve your complaint)`

@export By when must I ask the Commissioner to refer my complaint to the Civil and Administrative Tribunal for a hearing (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) ss 81, 86)? Within 21 days after receiving the Commissioner's notice that conciliation has ended, or by the extended day if the Commissioner extended the time. A representative complaint is not heard by the Tribunal.
GIVEN `a representative complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a representative complaint by an organisation about systemic discrimination
      `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the Commissioner's notice that conciliation had ended without resolving the complaint, and that you can ask for referral to the Tribunal
      `was the time extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner extended the time to ask
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day as extended (any date if not extended)
GIVETH A `Referral deadline`
`By when must I ask for a Tribunal hearing` MEANS
    `s 81 -- the referral deadline` `a representative complaint` `the day I received the notice` `was the time extended` `the extended last day`

@export If I ask on a given day for my complaint to be referred to the Tribunal, is that in time (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) ss 81, 87)? In time, the Commissioner must refer it; too late, the complaint lapses and you cannot complain again about the same conduct.
GIVEN `a representative complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a representative complaint by an organisation about systemic discrimination
      `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the Commissioner's notice that conciliation had ended without resolving the complaint
      `was the time extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner extended the time to ask
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day as extended (any date if not extended)
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask, or will ask, the Commissioner to refer the complaint
GIVETH A `Referral outcome`
`Is my request for a Tribunal hearing in time if made on this day` MEANS
    `s 81 -- the referral outcome` `a representative complaint` `the day I received the notice` `was the time extended` `the extended last day` `the day I ask`

@export Can the Tribunal order the respondent to pay me this amount of compensation (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 88)? Only if it finds the conduct substantiated (otherwise it must dismiss the complaint), and only up to the maximum prescribed by regulation, for loss or damage caused by the conduct, including offence, embarrassment, humiliation and intimidation. The Tribunal may also order the respondent not to repeat the conduct, to redress the loss (for example by employing, reinstating or promoting you), to apologise or retract (s 89), and may void an agreement.
GIVEN `found substantiated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has found the prohibited conduct alleged in your complaint substantiated
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of compensation, in dollars
      `the prescribed maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum amount prescribed by the Anti-Discrimination Regulations, in dollars (not deposited with this encoding; look it up)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Tribunal order this compensation` MEANS
    `s 88 -- the Tribunal may order this compensation` `found substantiated` `the amount` `the prescribed maximum`

@export By when must I appeal to the Supreme Court against the Tribunal's decision (Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) s 106)? Within 28 days after the day of the decision or order; or, if the Tribunal did not give written reasons at the time and you asked for them, within 28 days after the day you received them. The appeal may be on law, fact, or both.
GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal made its decision or order
      `were written reasons given then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal gave written reasons at the time of the decision or order
      `did I ask for written reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you later asked the Tribunal for written reasons
      `the day I received them` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the written reasons (any date if not)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I appeal` MEANS
    `s 106 -- the last day to appeal` `the day of the decision` `were written reasons given then` `did I ask for written reasons` `the day I received them`
